%N A401709 a(n) = sigma(n)/d, where d is the largest divisor d of sigma(n) that is relatively prime with n.
%H A401709 Antti Karttunen, <a href="/A401709/b401709.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A401709 <a href="/index/Si#SIGMAN">Index entries for sequences related to sigma(n)</a>.
%F A401709 a(n) = A000203(n) / A401375(n).
%F A401709 a(n) = A009194(n) * A401710(n).
%F A401709 Apparently, A306682(n)|a(n), for all n.
%o A401709 (PARI) A401709(n) = { my(s=sigma(n)); fordiv(s,d,if(1==gcd(s/d,n), return(d))); };
%Y A401709 Cf. A000203, A009194, A306682, A401375, A401710.
%Y A401709 Cf. A014567 (positions of 1's), A069059 (of terms > 1's), A105402 (of k where a(k) = A000203(k)).
